{"id":"mahabharata-12-057","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":57,"title":"सप्तपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 57 · The king's daily discipline","summary":{"en":"Bhishma tells that a king must be ever active, wary of all and trusting none too fully, and that he should keep a council of counsellors, spies and wise men. He describes the qualities that make a king beloved and the tests of ministers.","kn":"ರಾಜ ಸದಾ ಕ್ರಿಯಾಶೀಲ, ಎಲ್ಲರ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಜಾಗರೂಕ, ಯಾರನ್ನೂ ಅತಿಯಾಗಿ ನಂಬಬಾರದು, ಸಲಹೆಗಾರರು, ಗೂಢಚಾರರು, ಜ್ಞಾನಿಗಳ ಸಭೆ ಇಟ್ಟುಕೊಳ್ಳಬೇಕೆಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ರಾಜನನ್ನು ಪ್ರಿಯನಾಗಿಸುವ ಗುಣಗಳು, ಮಂತ್ರಿಗಳ ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆಗಳನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीष्म कहते हैं कि राजा सदा उद्यमी, सबसे सावधान और किसी पर अति विश्वास न करने वाला हो, और मन्त्रियों, गुप्तचरों तथा ज्ञानियों की सभा रखे। वे राजा को प्रिय बनाने वाले गुण और मन्त्रियों की परीक्षाएँ बताते हैं।","te":"రాజు ఎల్లప్పుడూ శ్రమించేవాడై, అందరి పట్ల జాగ్రత్తగా ఉండి, ఎవరినీ అతిగా నమ్మకూడదని, సలహాదారులు, గూఢచారులు, జ్ఞానుల సభ ఉంచుకోవాలని భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. రాజును ప్రియునిగా చేసే గుణాలను, మంత్రుల పరీక్షలను వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"மன்னன் எப்போதும் முயற்சியுடன், எல்லோரிடமும் எச்சரிக்கையுடன், எவரையும் மிகையாக நம்பாமல் இருக்க வேண்டும், ஆலோசகர், ஒற்றர், ஞானியரின் சபை வைத்திருக்க வேண்டும் என்று பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். மன்னனை விரும்பத்தக்கவனாக்கும் குணங்களையும் அமைச்சரின் சோதனைகளையும் விவரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"രാജാവ് എപ്പോഴും ഉണർവോടെയിരിക്കണമെന്നും, എല്ലാവരെയും സൂക്ഷിക്കണമെന്നും പൂർണ്ണമായി ആരെയും വിശ്വസിക്കരുതെന്നും ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; ഉപദേശകരുടെയും ചാരന്മാരുടെയും ജ്ഞാനികളുടെയും ഒരു സമിതി നിലനിർത്തണമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. രാജാവിനെ ജനങ്ങൾ സ്നേഹിക്കാൻ ഇടയാക്കുന്ന ഗുണങ്ങളും മന്ത്രിമാരുടെ പരീക്ഷകളും അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.57; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"नित्योद्युक्तेन वै राज्ञा भवितव्यं युधिष्ठिर ।\nप्रशाम्यते च राजा हि नारीवोद्यमवर्जितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king, Yudhishthira, must always be diligent; a king without effort is stilled and idle like a woman."}},{"n":2,"text":"भगवानुशना चाह श्लोकमत्र विशां पते ।\nतमिहैकमना राजन्गदतस्त्वं निबोध मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Venerable Ushanas also spoke a verse on this, lord of the people; listen to it, king, with one mind as I recite it."}},{"n":3,"text":"द्वावेतौ ग्रसते भूमिः सर्पो बिलशयानिव ।\nराजानं चाविरोद्धारं ब्राह्मणं चाप्रवासिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth swallows these two, as a snake swallows creatures lying in their holes: a king who does not resist, and a brahmin who does not travel."}},{"n":4,"text":"तदेतन्नरशार्दूल हृदि त्वं कर्तुमर्हसि ।\nसंधेयानपि संधत्स्व विरोध्यांश्च विरोधय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tiger among men, take this to heart: make peace even with those who can be won over, and set at odds those who ought to be opposed."}},{"n":5,"text":"सप्ताङ्गे यश्च ते राज्ये वैपरीत्यं समाचरेत् ।\nगुरुर्वा यदि वा मित्रं प्रतिहन्तव्य एव सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If anyone, whether a teacher or a friend, works against the seven limbs of your kingdom, he must be put down."}},{"n":6,"text":"मरुत्तेन हि राज्ञायं गीतः श्लोकः पुरातनः ।\nराज्याधिकारे राजेन्द्र बृहस्पतिमतः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"For long ago King Marutta recited an ancient verse on the duty of rule, which agrees with Brihaspati, king of kings."}},{"n":7,"text":"गुरोरप्यवलिप्तस्य कार्याकार्यमजानतः ।\nउत्पथप्रतिपन्नस्य परित्यागो विधीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even a teacher who is puffed up with pride, who knows not what to do and what not to do, and has gone down a wrong path, is to be cast aside."}},{"n":8,"text":"बाहोः पुत्रेण राज्ञा च सगरेणेह धीमता ।\nअसमञ्जाः सुतो ज्येष्ठस्त्यक्तः पौरहितैषिणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wise King Sagara, son of Bahu, wishing the good of the townsfolk, banished his eldest son Asamanja."}},{"n":9,"text":"असमञ्जाः सरय्वां प्राक्पौराणां बालकान्नृप ।\nन्यमज्जयदतः पित्रा निर्भर्त्स्य स विवासितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Asamanja used to drown the townsfolk's children in the Sarayu; so, rebuked by his father, he was exiled."}},{"n":10,"text":"ऋषिणोद्दालकेनापि श्वेतकेतुर्महातपाः ।\nमिथ्या विप्रानुपचरन्संत्यक्तो दयितः सुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage Uddalaka too cast off his beloved son Shvetaketu, the great ascetic, who was dishonestly serving brahmins."}},{"n":11,"text":"लोकरञ्जनमेवात्र राज्ञां धर्मः सनातनः ।\nसत्यस्य रक्षणं चैव व्यवहारस्य चार्जवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here the eternal duty of kings is to please the people, to guard the truth, and to keep affairs of state straightforward."}},{"n":12,"text":"न हिंस्यात्परवित्तानि देयं काले च दापयेत् ।\nविक्रान्तः सत्यवाक्क्षान्तो नृपो न चलते पथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should not seize others' wealth, and he should have what is due paid in time; a king who is valiant, truthful and forbearing does not stray from the path."}},{"n":13,"text":"गुप्तमन्त्रो जितक्रोधो शास्त्रार्थगतनिश्चयः ।\nधर्मे चार्थे च कामे च मोक्षे च सततं रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keeping his counsel secret, having mastered anger, certain of the meaning of the scriptures, he is always devoted to dharma, wealth, desire and liberation."}},{"n":14,"text":"त्रय्या संवृतरन्ध्रश्च राजा भवितुमर्हति ।\nवृजिनस्य नरेन्द्राणां नान्यत्संवरणात्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king deserves to be one who covers his weak points with the triple Veda; for kings there is no better covering of a fault than that."}},{"n":15,"text":"चातुर्वर्ण्यस्य धर्माश्च रक्षितव्या महीक्षिता ।\nधर्मसंकररक्षा हि राज्ञां धर्मः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The duties of the four classes must be guarded by the king, for guarding against the mixing of duties is the eternal duty of kings."}},{"n":16,"text":"न विश्वसेच्च नृपतिर्न चात्यर्थं न विश्वसेत् ।\nषाड्गुण्यगुणदोषांश्च नित्यं बुद्ध्यावलोकयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king should neither trust nor wholly distrust; he should always weigh with his mind the merits and demerits of the six-fold policy."}},{"n":17,"text":"द्विट्छिद्रदर्शी नृपतिर्नित्यमेव प्रशस्यते ।\nत्रिवर्गविदितार्थश्च युक्तचारोपधिश्च यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who sees his enemy's weak points is always praised, as is one who knows the meaning of the three aims and keeps spies and secret agents properly employed."}},{"n":18,"text":"कोशस्योपार्जनरतिर्यमवैश्रवणोपमः ।\nवेत्ता च दशवर्गस्य स्थानवृद्धिक्षयात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fond of gathering the treasury, like Yama and Vaishravana in stature, knowing the ten groups, and understanding what increases and diminishes his position,"}},{"n":19,"text":"अभृतानां भवेद्भर्ता भृतानां चान्ववेक्षकः ।\nनृपतिः सुमुखश्च स्यात्स्मितपूर्वाभिभाषिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"let him maintain those not yet maintained and look after those already maintained; let the king be pleasant-faced and speak with a smile first."}},{"n":20,"text":"उपासिता च वृद्धानां जिततन्द्रीरलोलुपः ।\nसतां वृत्ते स्थितमतिः सन्तो ह्याचारदर्शिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should wait on the elders, shake off sloth, be free of greed, and fix his mind on the conduct of the good, for the good are those who see right conduct."}},{"n":21,"text":"न चाददीत वित्तानि सतां हस्तात्कदाचन ।\nअसद्भ्यस्तु समादद्यात्सद्भ्यः संप्रतिपादयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should never take wealth from the hands of the good; he may take it from the wicked and give it to the good."}},{"n":22,"text":"स्वयं प्रहर्तादाता च वश्यात्मा वश्यसाधनः ।\nकाले दाता च भोक्ता च शुद्धाचारस्तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should himself strike and himself give, be master of himself and his means, give and enjoy at the proper time, and keep pure conduct."}},{"n":23,"text":"शूरान्भक्तानसंहार्यान्कुले जातानरोगिणः ।\nशिष्टाञ्शिष्टाभिसंबन्धान्मानिनो नावमानिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brave, devoted, incorruptible men born in good families and free of disease, well-bred and well-connected, proud but not scornful,"}},{"n":24,"text":"विद्याविदो लोकविदः परलोकान्ववेक्षकान् ।\nधर्मेषु निरतान्साधूनचलानचलानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"learned in lore and in the ways of the world, looking to the next world, steady in the duties, good people firm as mountains,"}},{"n":25,"text":"सहायान्सततं कुर्याद्राजा भूतिपुरस्कृतः ।\nतैस्तुल्यश्च भवेद्भोगैश्छत्रमात्राज्ञयाधिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"these a king, prizing prosperity, should always make his helpers; he should equal them in enjoyments and exceed them only in the umbrella and the command."}},{"n":26,"text":"प्रत्यक्षा च परोक्षा च वृत्तिश्चास्य भवेत्सदा ।\nएवं कृत्वा नरेन्द्रो हि न खेदमिह विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let his dealings be always both open and hidden; having done so, a king finds no distress here."}},{"n":27,"text":"सर्वातिशङ्की नृपतिर्यश्च सर्वहरो भवेत् ।\nस क्षिप्रमनृजुर्लुब्धः स्वजनेनैव बाध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who is suspicious of everyone, or who takes everything, will soon be crooked and greedy and be harassed by his own people."}},{"n":28,"text":"शुचिस्तु पृथिवीपालो लोकचित्तग्रहे रतः ।\nन पतत्यरिभिर्ग्रस्तः पतितश्चावतिष्ठते ॥","meaning":{"en":"But a pure king, intent on winning the hearts of the people, is not brought down even when seized by enemies, and if he falls he stands up again."}},{"n":29,"text":"अक्रोधनोऽथाव्यसनी मृदुदण्डो जितेन्द्रियः ।\nराजा भवति भूतानां विश्वास्यो हिमवानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who is free of anger and vice, mild in punishment and master of his senses, becomes trusted by creatures like the Himalaya."}},{"n":30,"text":"प्राज्ञो न्यायगुणोपेतः पररन्ध्रेषु तत्परः ।\nसुदर्शः सर्ववर्णानां नयापनयवित्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wise, endowed with justice, watchful for others' weak points, easy to see for all classes, and knowing right policy and wrong,"}},{"n":31,"text":"क्षिप्रकारी जितक्रोधः सुप्रसादो महामनाः ।\nअरोगप्रकृतिर्युक्तः क्रियावानविकत्थनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"quick in action, master of his anger, gracious, great-minded, healthy in nature, steady, active and not boastful,"}},{"n":32,"text":"आरब्धान्येव कार्याणि न पर्यवसितानि च ।\nयस्य राज्ञः प्रदृश्यन्ते स राजा राजसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the king in whose realm works are seen begun but not left unfinished is the best of kings."}},{"n":33,"text":"पुत्रा इव पितुर्गेहे विषये यस्य मानवाः ।\nनिर्भया विचरिष्यन्ति स राजा राजसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king in whose land people move fearless as sons in their father's house is the best of kings."}},{"n":34,"text":"अगूढविभवा यस्य पौरा राष्ट्रनिवासिनः ।\nनयापनयवेत्तारः स राजा राजसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king whose townsfolk and countryfolk hide no wealth and know right policy from wrong is the best of kings."}},{"n":35,"text":"स्वकर्मनिरता यस्य जना विषयवासिनः ।\nअसंघातरता दान्ताः पाल्यमाना यथाविधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is a king whose subjects who dwell in his land are devoted to their own work, not given to combination, self-restrained, and protected as the rule prescribes,"}},{"n":36,"text":"वश्या नेया विनीताश्च न च संघर्षशीलिनः ।\nविषये दानरुचयो नरा यस्य स पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"obedient, guidable and disciplined, not quarrelsome, and fond of giving in his realm."}},{"n":37,"text":"न यस्य कूटकपटं न माया न च मत्सरः ।\nविषये भूमिपालस्य तस्य धर्मः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a king's country where there is no fraud or deceit, no trickery and no jealousy, there is eternal dharma."}},{"n":38,"text":"यः सत्करोति ज्ञानानि नेयः पौरहिते रतः ।\nसतां धर्मानुगस्त्यागी स राजा राज्यमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king who honors the learned, is easily led, delights in the welfare of the townsfolk, follows the dharma of the good and is generous, deserves to rule."}},{"n":39,"text":"यस्य चारश्च मन्त्रश्च नित्यं चैव कृताकृते ।\nन ज्ञायते हि रिपुभिः स राजा राज्यमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king whose spies and counsel, and whose deeds done and undone, are never known to his enemies deserves to rule."}},{"n":40,"text":"श्लोकश्चायं पुरा गीतो भार्गवेण महात्मना ।\nआख्याते रामचरिते नृपतिं प्रति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"This verse was sung long ago by the great-souled Bhargava, descendant of Bharata, in telling the story of Rama, regarding the king."}},{"n":41,"text":"राजानं प्रथमं विन्देत्ततो भार्यां ततो धनम् ।\nराजन्यसति लोकस्य कुतो भार्या कुतो धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"First one should find a king, then a wife, then wealth; for if there is no king, how can the world have a wife or wealth?"}},{"n":42,"text":"तद्राजन्राजसिंहानां नान्यो धर्मः सनातनः ।\nऋते रक्षां सुविस्पष्टां रक्षा लोकस्य धारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, king, for lions among kings there is no other eternal duty than clear and open protection, for protection is the support of the world."}},{"n":43,"text":"प्राचेतसेन मनुना श्लोकौ चेमावुदाहृतौ ।\nराजधर्मेषु राजेन्द्र ताविहैकमनाः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Two verses were also recited by Manu, son of Prachetas, on the duties of kings; hear them with one mind, king of kings."}},{"n":44,"text":"षडेतान्पुरुषो जह्याद्भिन्नां नावमिवार्णवे ।\nअप्रवक्तारमाचार्यमनधीयानमृत्विजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man should abandon six, as one leaves a broken boat in the ocean: a teacher who does not speak, a priest who does not study,"}},{"n":45,"text":"अरक्षितारं राजानं भार्यां चाप्रियवादिनीम् ।\nग्रामकामं च गोपालं वनकामं च नापितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"a king who does not protect, a wife who speaks unkindly, a cowherd who longs for the village, and a barber who longs for the forest."}}]}]}